  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The disagreement is resolved as faithful-equivalent under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation and the applicable inherited rectangle-conservation convention. The round-trip judgment identifies missing operator evidence in its restricted packet, rather than a demonstrated mathematical mismatch. The supplied native supplement resolves those gaps by declarations applicable to the exact target instances.",
      "primary_evidence": "Attached printed pages 4–5; exact target type; D001–D004; native Real.volume_Ioc, MeasureTheory.integral_def, finite-vector integral_eq specialization, and FiniteRealVectorNormEvidence declarations."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The requested checks of measure, integration, norm, and exceptional regional-average inputs have been performed against the supplied declaration evidence. No disputed dependency remains unresolved for this target. This conclusion follows from the declarations and their actual instantiations, not from agreement with the direct judge or reuse hashes.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplement exposes real-volume normalization, restriction by intersection, integrability definitions, the L1 construction of the Bochner integral, extended-real conversion, and explicit equalities between the target's norm instances."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The evidence limitations supporting that classification are removed in the adjudicator packet. Both implications hold for the interpretation-qualified local numerical claim. This does not establish unqualified equivalence to every assertion in the surrounding source discussion.",
      "primary_evidence": "Section 1.2 explicitly bases the numerical mechanism on (1.10). Q7 separately selects conditional transfer of old-average and time-averaged face-flux errors. The target contains precisely that local construction and comparison."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D044 unclear",
      "resolution": "D044 selects the finite maximum absolute-component norm. The complete projection chain reaches Pi.seminormedAddGroup's finite supremum formula. Explicit native equalities identify the ring norm with both additive-group norms used elsewhere in the target, and identify their extended norms. Thus there is no hidden Euclidean norm, squared norm, or inconsistent integrability norm.",
      "primary_evidence": "Supplement span 'Exact finite-real-vector norm projections, coordinate bounds, extended norms, and scaling': Pi.seminormedRing, Pi.nonUnitalSeminormedRing, Pi.seminormedAddCommGroup, Pi.seminormedAddGroup; ring_norm_eq_addCommGroup_norm; ring_norm_eq_addGroup_norm; ring_norm_eq_sup; integral_enorm_eq_ring_norm; generic_integral_enorm_eq_ring_norm."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D061 unclear",
      "resolution": "D061 is the real Borel measure space with ordinary length-normalized volume. The native expansion identifies its selected instance, and the explicit volume theorem uses exactly Real.measureSpace. Its identification with the identity Stieltjes measure and its interval-mass formula establish the normalization needed here.",
      "primary_evidence": "Native Real.measurableSpace = borel Real; expanded Real.measureSpace; fully explicit Real.volume_eq_stieltjes_id and Real.volume_Ioc; Real.volume_real_Ioc_of_le. In particular, volume((a,b]) = ENNReal.ofReal(b-a)."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D091 unclear",
      "resolution": "ENNReal.toReal maps finite nonnegative values to their real values and infinity to zero. The exceptional infinity branch is irrelevant: the target uses only finite real intervals with strictly positive lengths. Their converted measures are exactly b-a and t-s, both positive.",
      "primary_evidence": "Native ENNReal.toNNReal = WithTop.untopD 0, ENNReal.toReal_ofReal, ENNReal.toReal_top; Real.volume_Ioc; target hypotheses a < b and s < t; D002's reciprocal converted-volume definition."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D101 unclear",
      "resolution": "The opaque wrapper is resolved by the supplied integral characterizations. On an integrable function into a complete codomain, the operator is the L1 integral, constructed by continuous extension of simple-function integration. The actual codomain Fin m → Real is complete, as also witnessed by the supplied native specialization. All four relevant fields are explicitly integrable, and their temporal flux difference is integrable. No substantive integral uses a fallback zero branch.",
      "primary_evidence": "MeasureTheory.integral_def and integral_eq; finite-real-vector specialization of integral_eq; L1.integralCLM and integralCLM'; simple-function integral sums and extension characterizations; target holdDensity, hnewDensity, hleftFlux, hrightFlux; D020 and D079."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "Conclusion completeness passes for the selected local claim under Q7. Both spatial averages, both temporal physical flux averages, the numerical update, the exact weighted error identity, and the conditional next-step estimate are present. The two explicit regional-average bridges are sufficient certifications; the other two averages already use the same normalized-integral definition. The surrounding discontinuity discussion is inherited context, not an additional theorem this target must prove.",
      "primary_evidence": "All ten target conjuncts; D001, D002, D004; attached Section 1.2 definition of cell averages and edge-flux modification; Q7's independent-error interpretation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Operator interpretation passes. D001 requires ordering, integrability, and equality to D004; D004 divides an oriented interval integral by interval length; D002 divides a restricted integral by region measure; D003 subtracts duration/volume times outward numerical flux. The external arithmetic, measure, integral, norm, and coercion declarations preserve those meanings at the target's concrete instances.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001–D114 and the native supplement, particularly restriction evaluation laws, D079's orientation, real interval measures, complete-codomain integral characterization, and exact finite-vector norm-instance equalities."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Exceptional-case handling passes for the actual target. Positive finite interval measures avoid zero or infinite normalization; explicit integrability and codomain completeness avoid integral collapse. Negative error bounds merely have unsatisfiable antecedents and do not make the universally conditional result vacuous. Equal face labels remain permissible algebraic instances. Spatial endpoint evaluation remains conditional on the supplied histories satisfying physical balance; no representative-independent trace theorem is asserted.",
      "primary_evidence": "Target positivity and integrability premises; D002–D004; native integral_def, ENNReal conversion and volume_Ioc; absence of a face-distinctness premise; literal flux(q a τ) and flux(q b τ) in hphysicalBalance and the error comparisons."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N02 unclear",
      "resolution": "Norm semantics pass under Q7. Every error uses the same unsquared maximum absolute-component norm, with ordinary real scalar homogeneity. For m > 0, its upper-bound predicate is equivalent to the corresponding absolute bound on every component. This is a concrete realization of the selected conditional comparison, not a norm specified by LeVeque.",
      "primary_evidence": "Fully explicit target NormedRing.toNorm/Pi.normedRing applications; native ring_norm_le_iff_abs_of_pos, ring_norm_smul, and norm-instance equalities; printed Section 1.2 supplies no norm; Q7 forbids attributing a chosen norm or order to the book."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The implication is yes under the recorded Q7 interpretation and applicable inherited rectangle convention. After resolving the operators, the translated proposition supplies actual volume averages, the local conservative numerical construction from old cell data, and the selected conditional accuracy transfer. Conservation remains inherited input; this implication does not claim to derive physical solutionhood from a conditional numerical theorem.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001–D004; resolved D044, D061, D091, D101; target update, weighted error identity, and final conditional inequality; attached Section 1.2 and its reference to (1.10)."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The implication is yes under the recorded conventions. Put w=b-a and d=t-s. Rectangle balance gives w(A_t-A_s)=d(F_L-F_R). Replacing the temporal physical flux averages by the numerical face outputs gives U_new=U+(d/w)(G_L-G_R). Subtracting yields w(U_new-A_t)=w(U-A_s)+d((G_L-F_L)-(G_R-F_R)). Triangle inequality and positive scaling give the exact stated bound. The other conjuncts follow from normalization, integrability, positivity, and unfolding the update.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.10)'s endpoint signs; applicable finite-rectangle interpretation; Q7's temporal face-flux comparison; D001–D004; native length-measure normalization and maximum-norm scaling characterizations."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q7 interpretation and the applicable inherited rectangle-conservation convention, the target represents the selected local finite-volume mechanism and conditional accuracy statement. Its exact averages are physical integrals divided by positive cell width; its numerical rule reads approximate old cell data; its update uses left inflow minus right outflow; and its final conjunct transfers independent old-state and temporal physical face-flux error bounds to the next cell-average error. The supplement establishes the actual measure, integral, and maximum-norm meanings. Physical conservation is retained as inherited context, not independently proved by this implication. No global PDE theorem, universal trace convention, accurate-rule existence, or unconditional accuracy assertion follows."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under Q7 and the locally applicable inherited rectangle convention, finite conservation and temporal averaging yield the exact reference cell-average update. The numerical counterpart and subtraction give the displayed weighted error identity with precisely the target's signs and duration/width coefficient. Triangle inequality in the concrete maximum norm yields the bound for every valid triple of independent error bounds. Ordered finite intervals, integrability, and the supplied measure/integral characterizations give the remaining average certifications and volume identifications. This is a derivation for arbitrary admissible local data and does not require global conservation or classical smoothness. The printed passage alone does not specify this quantitative comparison; the implication is explicitly interpretation-qualified."
    }
  },
  "classification": "faithful-equivalent",
  "accepted": true,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The printed source leaves numerical flux accuracy qualitative and does not select a norm, tolerance, accuracy order, discrete formula, or time-integration prescription. Acceptance depends on the separately recorded Q7 interpretation.",
    "The printed discontinuity discussion leaves temporal and endpoint-trace conventions implicit. The inherited receipt supports rectangle conservation here but does not establish representative-independent face evaluation or authorize arbitrary global solution extensions.",
    "Source bytes, rendering hashes, and environment provenance were supplied by the orchestrator. I inspected the attached images and inline declarations without independently recomputing hashes or executing Lean."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "interpretation-qualified-acceptance",
      "evidence": "Section 1.2 describes approximate cell averages and edge fluxes qualitatively. Q7 separately selects independent old-average and time-averaged physical face-flux errors yielding a next-step bound.",
      "impact": "Acceptance is equivalence to that interpreted local claim. It must not be reported as a quantitative theorem explicitly printed in the book or as a detailed convention literally selected by the user."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "dependency-gaps-resolved",
      "evidence": "The native supplement identifies the exact real measure and interval masses, the integrable complete-codomain Bochner integral, extended-real conversion, and equality of the target's ring, additive, and extended norm instances.",
      "impact": "The blind and round-trip operator uncertainties do not remain substantive obstacles for this target. Reuse provenance alone was not used as semantic justification."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "nonvacuity-and-applicability",
      "evidence": "Choose m=1, Cell=Unit, Face=Bool, a=s=0, b=t=1, q=0, flux=0, numericalOld=0, and a rule returning 0 on the left and 1 on the right. All physical premises hold, U_new=-1, and bounds (0,0,1) give an attained error bound of 1. A bounded time-independent spatial step with zero physical flux also satisfies the premises.",
      "impact": "The theorem admits nonzero numerical error and discontinuous states. Positive lengths and dimension exclude degenerate normalization and empty-vector collapse. No additional smoothness premise reduces the intended applicability."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "local-conditional-scope",
      "evidence": "The target assumes one rectangle balance and four local integrability conditions. Its rule is arbitrary, and face labels have no mesh structure. The error comparisons explicitly pair numerical outputs with the two physical endpoint histories.",
      "impact": "The theorem certifies a local conditional update comparison, not mesh validity, global evolution, accurate-flux construction, stability, or convergence. Its redundant certifications and exact error identity do not warrant classification as faithful-stronger."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached source pages confirms volume-normalized cell averages, endpoint-flux conservation, and the nonsmooth motivation. Inspection of the exact target and dependency declarations confirms the same local objects and signs under the separately recorded conventions. The native supplement resolves each consequential gap identified by the blind translator and round-trip judge, including the precise norm-instance compatibility and the effective domain of integration and normalization. Both implications follow by the local balance and update algebra, with a nonvacuous attained-error example and no imposed classical smoothness. The resulting classification is faithful-equivalent only for the interpretation-qualified local claim; the original printed ambiguities and the inherited receipt's scope remain preserved."
}
